READ: `instances_with_a_zero_witness` > 0 is the non-vacuity control --
identically-zero witnesses DO occur in this sample, so (R3) is not
trivially satisfied here.  `CONSULTS_A_ZERO_WITNESS` = 0 says Theorem
CI's proof never reads one of them, i.e. (R3) is not among its
hypotheses.  The split of the consulted keys shows why: those with
c_0 != 0 need only that the quantity is nonzero at alpha = 0; the
rest are exactly (R2)'s four D's per apex, which (R2) itself asserts
are not identically zero.
